# Flutter Rules

Flutter is used for mobile and web.

Rules:
- Use feature-first structure.
- Use Riverpod for state management.
- Use GoRouter for routing.
- Use Dio for API calls.
- Widgets must not call APIs directly.
- Data layer handles API calls.
- Application layer handles state/controllers.
- Presentation layer contains UI.
- Each feature should support mobile and web layouts.
- Use shared widgets from shared/widgets.
- Add loading, empty, and error states.

Before creating UI:
- Search shared widgets first.
- Read docs/frontend/reusable-widgets.md.
- Read docs/frontend/state-management.md for providers/controllers/repositories.
- Read docs/07-theme-system.md for colors/theme.
- Verify feature status in docs/08-implementation-status.md.

When adding reusable widgets:
- Update docs/frontend/reusable-widgets.md.

When changing theme, tokens, colors, or palettes:
- Update docs/07-theme-system.md.

When changing providers/controllers/repositories:
- Update docs/frontend/state-management.md.

If unsure whether docs are needed, ask explicitly.
